    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d283">

                <pb facs="0326" n="261" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg261"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.84/60: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-04T20:30:00+02:35">May 4, 1936—8:30
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 4—1:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>284. Many thanks for your 180 and 181.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d283-f1"/> Hope the
                    Department is not unduly alarmed but we would so much like to save the Legation
                    if at all possible.</p>
                <p>Reference your 182, inter-Legation radio communications were being arranged but
                    unexpectedly sudden outbreak of disturbances prevented completion.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
